WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.280
Carbon per kilowatt-hour rises
and falls through the day.

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.750
When a long job can wait,
your coding agent hands it to Tidegap.

3
00:00:10.885 --> 00:00:16.785
Tidegap reads the grid forecast for your region
and picks the cleanest hour before your deadline.

4
00:00:17.085 --> 00:00:23.145
Nothing to babysit. At six, the job starts
by itself, with the context of your session.

5
00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:28.395
When it's done, Tidegap tells you:
in Telegram, on your Mac or in your browser.

6
00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:33.905
In the morning, the answer is waiting,
with the clean hour it ran in.

7
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:40.885
To start, paste one prompt into Claude Code,
Codex, Cursor or any MCP host.

8
00:00:41.185 --> 00:00:44.555
Tidegap. Tasks that can wait,
wait for clean power.
